    "Condition : 1 - 11.\tRECCOMENDATION\r\n\r\nCertificate of Lawfulness be GRANTED\r\n\r\n12.\tREASONS\r\n\r\nThe London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 2nd December, 2003, the erection of a roof extension that adds 19.57m3 to the volume of the original dwelling, as shown on drawing numbers LR3184/01/02/03/04 dated November 2003 as lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act and therefore does not require planning permission for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe proposed roof extension falls within Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
